{DisplayName}: {ProjectName}
================================

This complete project uses SDK template {TemplateId} and the exact SDK,
Contract and RustToolsProfile identities in r4os-project.json. Those pins
contain no host workspace paths. Select the separate component directories:

  ./Build.sh -SdkRoot /SDK -ContractRoot /CONTRACT -ToolsRoot /TOOLS -InstallRoot /install -CacheRoot /cache

Windows: Build.bat with the same parameters. Both call this project's Build.ps1
and the SDK-owned PS7 driver. No complete R4OS workspace or Settings.R4S.
Cargo.lock is included; builds are offline/locked. module.R4MF owns module
class, identity, imports, version, resources and target. Change that manifest
for module facts; Cargo's crate identity remains separate.

The output is build/{ProjectName}.R4X with build.json source/tool/container
provenance. Copy the container to its manifest TARGET in R4OS. Console apps
print a marker and return0. GUI apps need the regular desktop host, display
a window, wait for events and close normally. Services use SERVMAN:

  SERVMAN INSTALL {ProjectName} C:\path\{ProjectName}.R4X
  SERVMAN START {ProjectName}
  SERVMAN STATUS {ProjectName}
  SERVMAN STOP {ProjectName}

Only the template's actual class applies; read module.R4MF. Service endpoints
register under that module name, wait on bounded deadlines and unregister on
stop. No native Rust compiler is installed in R4OS by these host tools.
See SDK/Rust/README.txt for the profile, supported scope and evidence limits.
